course: dictionary
lesson: 10397
title: A tribunal is a kind of court
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tribunal is a special kind of court, or any group with the power to judge someone. It is often set up to decide one particular kind of problem. «An employment tribunal is a kind of court for work disputes, such as being sacked unfairly or not being paid what is owed.» So an employment tribunal hears arguments about work.
explain: The words around a word give you clues. Here, the sentence explains the word for you in brackets: «A tribunal (a kind of court that settles disagreements) decided the airline had to honour what its chatbot had said.» Settles disagreements tells you that a tribunal is a place where arguments are decided.
explain: Some tribunals judge very serious crimes, such as war crimes. In stories, a tribunal can sound frightening, because someone may have to stand before it. When you meet a new word, put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A tribunal is a kind of court, or a group with the power to judge someone.
fact: An employment tribunal is a court that settles work disputes, such as being sacked unfairly.
fact: A war crimes tribunal is a court set up to judge serious crimes such as war crimes.
fact: «Appear before a tribunal» means stand in front of it to be judged.
fact: «Go to a tribunal» means take your problem or case to that kind of court.
exercise: «An employment tribunal is a kind of court for work disputes.» What is an employment tribunal for? | Counting the stars at night | Painting pictures in a gallery | Choosing what to have for school dinner | *Arguments about work, such as being sacked unfairly
exercise: «A tribunal decided the airline had to honour what its chatbot had said.» What does a tribunal do? | *Decides disagreements and judges problems | Plays football at the weekend | Sells tickets on planes | Builds houses for families
exercise: Which word is the name for a court or group that judges problems? | airline | customer | *tribunal | chatbot
test: Workers who think they were sacked unfairly may take their case to what? | A shop counter | A bus stop | A swimming pool | *An employment tribunal
test: What might a war crimes tribunal do? | *Judge serious crimes committed during a war | Give out prizes for sport | Build new roads after a storm | Choose the best school for children
exam: Lena reads, «Mia had to appear before a tribunal,» and feels scared. Why does this sentence sound frightening? | Tribunals only give out sweets, so Mia must be in trouble | Appear means to disappear, so Mia is lost | A tribunal is a kind of football match | *A tribunal is a court where someone is judged, and they must stand in front of it
